      "Question and scope",
      "The scope is one defined population of vendor scorecard cases observed from first request through verified close in the vendor scorecard. Exclude a reopened case only when the reopening did not create a new requirement; keep the exclusion count and reason. Write the primary measure and one supporting measure; a measure without a denominator or observation window is not ready. Record the exclusions in advance so a difficult case cannot be removed after the result is known. If the case moved between owners, include both owner periods in the review note and name the handoff time.\n\nWrite the primary question and one supporting question, then stop; a long list of questions usually hides an undefined unit. A count without a denominator is not a measurement, especially when the queue changes size during the day. Write the primary measure and one supporting measure; a measure without a denominator or observation window is not ready. Separate the operational question from the compliance question; this method does not certify either outcome. Keep the review note with the case so the next sampler does not have to reconstruct the decision from memory.",
      "Population and unit",
