      "Definitions and measures",
      "A pause should have a reason, an owner, and a review date; otherwise it is an unowned case with a different label. Record the version of the vendor scorecard and the program management portal snapshot used for each case. A completeness measure should name the required fields and the evidence state; an overall percentage is not reproducible. If two reviewers disagree, preserve both classifications until the definition is clarified. If the evidence is sensitive, record the approved reference and access path rather than copying the content.\n\nA pause should have a reason, an owner, and a review date; otherwise it is an unowned case with a different label. Keep the original text and the coded value together so a reviewer can check the classification. If a case is outside the scope rule, record the rule and the date of exclusion rather than removing it silently. State how duplicate, cancelled, and reopened cases enter the numerator and denominator. The note should distinguish what was observed, what was inferred, and what still needs an owner decision.",
      "Data dictionary and evidence",
